%description -n texlive-alnumsec
This package allows you to use alphanumeric section numbering, for instance "A.
Introduction ... III. International Law". Its output is similar to alphanum,
but you can use the standard LaTeX sectioning commands, so that it is possible
to switch numbering schemes easily. Greek letters, double letters (bb) and
different delimiters around them are supported.

%package -n texlive-alphalph
Summary:        Convert numbers to letters
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(infwarerr.sty)
Requires:       tex(intcalc.sty)

%description -n texlive-alphalph
Provides commands \alphalph and \AlphAlph. They are like \number but the
expansion consists of lowercase and uppercase letters respectively (1 to a, 26
to z, 27 to aa, 52 to zz, 53 to ba, 702 to zz, 703 to aaa, etc.). Can be used
as a replacement for LaTeX's \@alph and \@Alph macros.

%package -n texlive-alterqcm
Summary:        Multiple choice questionnaires in two column tables
Version:        svn59265
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(array.sty)
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
