Requires:       tex(tocloft.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xtab.sty)

%description -n texlive-book-of-common-prayer
This a package for the typesetting of liturgical documents in the style of the
1979 "Book of Common Prayer". It provides macros for common liturgical
situations (e.g. versicle and response, longer prayers, etc.). This package is
designed to work with the Sabon font, but it is not necessary to run the
macros.

%package -n texlive-bookcover
Summary:        A class for book covers and dust jackets
Version:        svn77334
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bookcover-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bookcover-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-bookcover
This class helps typesetting book covers and dust jackets.

%package -n texlive-bookest
Summary:        Extended book class
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bookest-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bookest-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-bookest
The class extends the standard book class, in the areas of colour scheme
management, document layout, headings and footers, front page layout, and other
minor items.

%package -n texlive-booklet
Summary:        Aids for printing simple booklets
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-booklet-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-booklet-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-booklet
Pages of a document processed with the booklet package will be reordered and
scaled so that they can be printed as four pages per physical sheet of paper,
two pages per side. The resulting sheets will, when folded in half, assemble
into a booklet. Instructions on producing the manual itself as a booklet are
included.

%package -n texlive-booktabstabular
Summary:        Automatic application of the booktabs style
Version:        svn78551
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(booktabs.sty)

%description -n texlive-booktabstabular
The booktabstabular package provides wrapper environments around tabular and
tabular* that insert \toprule at the beginning, \bottomrule at the end, and
locally remap the legacy \hline and \cline commands to their booktabs
equivalents \midrule and \cmidrule. It also provides commands to temporarily
override the standard tabular and tabular* environments so that existing
documents can opt into this behaviour without rewriting each table.

%package -n texlive-boolexpr
Summary:        A boolean expression evaluator and a switch command
Version:        svn17830
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-boolexpr-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-boolexpr-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-boolexpr
The \boolexpr macro evaluates boolean expressions in a purely expandable way.
\boolexpr{ A \OR B \AND C } expands to 0 if the logical expression is TRUE. A,
B, C may be: numeric expressions such as: x=y, x<>y, x>y or x<y; - boolean
switches: \iftrue 0\else 1\fi; - conditionals: \ifcsname whatsit\endcsname
0\else 1\fi; - another \boolexpr: \boolexpr{ D \OR E \AND F }: \boolexpr may be
used with \ifcase: \ifcase\boolexpr{ A \OR B \AND C } What to do if true \else
What to do if false \fi The \switch command (which is also expandable) has the
form: \switch \case{<boolean expression>} ... \case{<boolean expression>} ...
... \otherwise ... \endswitch

%package -n texlive-bophook
Summary:        Provides an At-Begin-Page hook
Version:        svn17062
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bophook-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bophook-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-bophook
Using the \AtBeginPage hook, you can add material in the background of a page.
\PageLayout can be used to give page makeup commands to be executed on every
page (e.g., depending on the page style).

%package -n texlive-boxedminipage
Summary:        Framed minipages of a specified total width (text and frame combined)
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-boxedminipage
The package essentially just wraps a minipage within an \fbox. However, while
\fbox{\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}...\end{minipage}} juts out into the margin,
\begin{boxedminipage}...\end{boxedminipage} does not. Instead, it subtracts the
frame's dimensions from the specified dimensions of the minipage before
typesetting the minipage. Note: The package was formerly known as
boxedminipage2e and now replaces Mario Wolczko's earlier boxedminipage package.

%package -n texlive-boxhandler
Summary:        Flexible Captioning and Deferred Box/List Printing
Version:        svn76790
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-boxhandler-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-boxhandler-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(pbox.sty)

%description -n texlive-boxhandler
The package allows the user to optimise presentation of LaTeX tables and
figures. Boxhandler will lay out table and figure captions with a variety of
stylistic appearances, and will also allow figures and tables to be "wrapped"
in a manner consistent with many business and government documents. For a
document that might appear in different venues with different formatting,
boxhandler permits the creation of a LaTeX source document that can, with a
single-line change in the source code, produce an output that has very
different layout from the baseline configuration, not only in terms of caption
style, but more importantly in terms of the locations where figures, tables and
lists appear (or not) in the document. Deferral routines also allow one to keep
all figure and table data in a separate source file, while nonetheless
producing a document with figures and tables appearing in the desired location.

%package -n texlive-bracketkey
Summary:        Produce bracketed identification keys
Version:        svn17129
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bracketkey-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bracketkey-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(coolstr.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(xifthen.sty)

%description -n texlive-bracketkey
The package provides an environment bracketkey for use when producing lists of
species.

%package -n texlive-braket
Summary:        Dirac bra-ket and set notations
Version:        svn77682
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-braket-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-braket-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-braket
Provides macros to typeset bra-ket notation, as well as set specifiers, with a
single ("|") or a double ("||" or ("\|") vertical bar specifier in between two
bracketed parts. Each macro comes in a fixed-size version and an expanding
version. If the package finds itself operating under e-tex, it uses the
extended primitive \middle for more reliable results

%package -n texlive-breakurl
Summary:        Line-breakable \url-like links in hyperref when compiling via dvips/ps2pdf
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-breakurl-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-breakurl-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ifpdf.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-breakurl
This package provides a command much like hyperref's \url that typesets a URL
using a typewriter-like font. However, if the dvips driver is being used, the
original \url doesn't allow line breaks in the middle of the created link: the
link comes in one atomic piece. This package allows such line breaks in the
generated links.

%package -n texlive-bubblesort
Summary:        Bubble sorts a list
Version:        svn56070
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)

%description -n texlive-bubblesort
This package sorts a list of TeX items {item 1}...{item k} in "increasing"
order where "increasing" is determined by a comparator macro. By default it
sorts real numbers with the usual meaning of "increasing" but some other
examples are discussed in the documentation. A second macro is included which
sorts one list and applies the same permutation to a second list.

%package -n texlive-bullcntr
Summary:        Display list item counter as regular pattern of bullets
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bullcntr-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bullcntr-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-bullcntr
The bullcntr package defines the command bullcntr, which may be thought of as
an analogue of the \fnsymbol command: like the latter, it displays the value of
a counter lying between 1 and 9, but uses, for the purpose, a regular pattern
of bullets.

%package -n texlive-bxcalc
Summary:        Extend the functionality of the calc package
Version:        svn78793
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)

%description -n texlive-bxcalc
This package bundle consists of the following packages: bxcalcize: To make calc
expressions available in more places. bxcalcux: To add user-defined units to
the calc syntax. In addition, this bundle provides the bxcalc package, which
simply loads the above-mentioned packages internally.

%package -n texlive-bxdpx-beamer
Summary:        Dvipdfmx extras for use with beamer
Version:        svn41813
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bxdpx-beamer-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bxdpx-beamer-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-bxdpx-beamer
The package is a driver to support beamer Navigation symbols and \framezoomed
regions when using dvipdfmx as PDF generator (e.g., as part of e-pTeX). The
package does not define any 'user' commands.

%package -n texlive-bxdvidriver
Summary:        Enables specifying a driver option effective only in DVI output
Version:        svn78793
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bxdvidriver-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bxdvidriver-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ifluatex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifpdf.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifvtex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifxetex.sty)
Requires:       tex(pdftexcmds.sty)

%description -n texlive-bxdvidriver
This single-function package enables authors to specify a global driver option
(dvips, dvipdfmx, etc) which is applied only when the engine outputs a DVI
file. It is useful to create special document- templates that can be compiled
in both PDF-mode and DVI-mode.

%package -n texlive-bxenclose
Summary:        Enclose the document body with some pieces of code
Version:        svn40213
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bxenclose-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bxenclose-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-bxenclose
The package enables authors to designate in the preamble to make the document
body enclosed with the given pieces of code. As is known, there are already
various mechanisms provided by LaTeX kernel or packages that attach hooks at
the beginning and end of documents.

%package -n texlive-bxnewfont
Summary:        Enhanced \newfont command
Version:        svn44173
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bxnewfont-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bxnewfont-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)

%description -n texlive-bxnewfont
This package provides a new command \newfontx. It is similar to the old (and
deprecated) command \newfont in function, but is more compatible with NFSS. In
particular, one can safely change font size after invoking a font command
defined by \newfontx. The new command will be useful to users who know much of
the old \newfont command, but are unfamiliar with the details of NFSS.

%package -n texlive-bxpapersize
Summary:        Synchronize output paper size with layout paper size
Version:        svn78793
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bxpapersize-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bxpapersize-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(atbegshi.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifluatex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifpdf.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifptex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifvtex.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifxetex.sty)
Requires:       tex(pxatbegshi.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-bxpapersize
As is well known, in LaTeX processing layout paper size specified by document
class options is not automatically applied to output paper size. This package
enables LaTeX authors to synchronize both kinds of paper sizes.

%package -n texlive-bxpdfver
Summary:        Specify version and compression level of output PDF files
Version:        svn74105
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-bxpdfver-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-bxpdfver-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(atbegshi.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)

%description -n texlive-bxpdfver
This package enables users to specify in their sources the following settings
on the PDF document to output: PDF version (1.4, 1.5 etc.); whether or not to
compress streams; whether or not to use object streams. This package supports
all major PDF-output engines and dvipdfmx.

%package -n texlive-bxtexlogo
Summary:        Additional TeX-family logos
Version:        svn78849
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-bxtexlogo
The hologo package provides many useful logos of popular (and not so popular)
TeX-family software. However, its interface is a bit cumbersome because you
must type \hologo{BibTeX} instead of \BibTeX. This package makes it possible to
import some of the logos provided by hologo as single commands, such as
\BibTeX. Additionally, the package provides logos of some TeX-family software
that is popular mainly in Japan. These logos can be imported in the same way as
those provided by the \hologo command. bxtexlogo depends on hologo and cjhebrew
(if \logoAleph and \logoLamed are used).

%package -n texlive-calcage
Summary:        Calculate the age of something, in years
Version:        svn27725
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-calcage-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-calcage-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(datenumber.sty)
Requires:       tex(fnumprint.sty)
Requires:       tex(fp.sty)
Requires:       tex(kvoptions.sty)
Requires:       tex(xifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-calcage
The package calculates the age of someone or something in years. Internally it
uses the datenumber package to calculate the age in days; conversion from days
to years is then performed, taking care of leap years and such odd things.

%package -n texlive-calctab
Summary:        Language for numeric tables
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-calctab-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-calctab-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(booktabs.sty)
Requires:       tex(eurosym.sty)
Requires:       tex(fltpoint.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(numprint.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)
Requires:       tex(xstring.sty)

%description -n texlive-calctab
The calctab package helps the user to typeset a kind of economic table such as
invoices, expense notes and liquidation, or other tabular material with a
values column. The code computes sum and percentage with floating point numeric
methods (using the fltpoint package) and builds the render table task.

%package -n texlive-calculator
Summary:        Use LaTeX as a scientific calculator
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-calculator-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-calculator-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-calculator
The calculator and calculus packages define several instructions which allow us
to realise algebraic operations and to evaluate elementary functions and
derivatives in our documents. The package's main goal is to define the
arithmetic and functional calculations needed in the author's package xpicture,
but the numeric abilities of "calculator" and "calculus" may be useful in other
contexts.

%package -n texlive-calculatoritems
Summary:        Insert menus/items for classic calculators
Version:        svn76037
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(amssymb.sty)
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(fontspec.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(inlinegraphicx.sty)
Requires:       tex(listofitems.sty)
Requires:       tex(settobox.sty)
Requires:       tex(simplekv.sty)
Requires:       tex(tcolorbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(tikz.sty)
Requires:       tex(xstring.sty)

%description -n texlive-calculatoritems
Insert inline (based on tcolorbox, graphicx and calc packages) items/menus for
classic calculators (numworks, casio, texas instruments, hp).

%package -n texlive-calrsfs
Summary:        Copperplate calligraphic letters in LaTeX
Version:        svn77682
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-calrsfs-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-calrsfs-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-calrsfs
Provides a maths interface to the rsfs fonts.

%package -n texlive-cals
Summary:        Multipage tables with wide range of features
Version:        svn43003
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cals-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cals-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-cals
The package is a set of macros to typeset multipage tables with repeatable
headers and footers, with cells spanned over rows and columns. Decorations are
supported: padding, background color, width of separation rules. The code is
compatible with multicol and bidi.

%package -n texlive-calxxxx-yyyy
Summary:        Print a calendar for a group of years
Version:        svn77222
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-calxxxx-yyyy-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-calxxxx-yyyy-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-calxxxx-yyyy
The package prints a calendar for two or more years, according to a language
selection. The package is also "culture dependent" in the sense that it will
start weeks according to local rules: e.g., weeks conventionally start on
Monday in the English-speaking world. The package requires array, babel, and
geometry.

%package -n texlive-cancel
Summary:        Place lines through maths formulae
Version:        svn77682
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cancel-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cancel-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-cancel
A package to draw diagonal lines ("cancelling" a term) and arrows with limits
(cancelling a term "to a value") through parts of maths formulae.

%package -n texlive-canoniclayout
Summary:        Create canonical page layouts with memoir
Version:        svn64889
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-canoniclayout-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-canoniclayout-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)

%description -n texlive-canoniclayout
A canonic text layout has specified relations to a circle inscribed within the
enclosing page. The package allows the user to use a canonic layout with the
memoir class.

%package -n texlive-capt-of
Summary:        Captions on more than floats
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-capt-of-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-capt-of-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-capt-of
Defines a command \captionof for putting a caption to something that's not a
float. Note that the caption package includes a \captionof command that is an
extension of that provided by this package.

%package -n texlive-captcont
Summary:        Retain float number across several floats
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-captcont-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-captcont-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-captcont
The captcont package provides the ability to continue the numbering in your
float environment (figure, table, etc.) with minimal overhead. This package
adds three commands: \caption*, \captcont, and \captcont*. Along with the
\caption command, these give full control over the caption numbering, caption
text and the entries in the list-of pages. The \caption and \captcont commands
generate list-of page entries. The \caption and \caption* commands increment
the figure or table counter. Captcont also fully supports the subfigure
package.

%package -n texlive-captdef
Summary:        Declare free-standing \caption commands
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-captdef-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-captdef-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-captdef
The \DeclareCaption command defines a class of caption command associated with
the counter specified to the command. These commands are free-standing (i.e.,
don't need to be inside a float environment). The package uses \DeclareCaption
to define \figcaption and \tabcaption, which can be used outside figure or
table environments.

%package -n texlive-carbohydrates
Summary:        Carbohydrate molecules with chemfig
Version:        svn39000
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-carbohydrates-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-carbohydrates-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(chemfig.sty)
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)

%description -n texlive-carbohydrates
This package offers macros that make the preparation of exercise sheets for
teaching carbohydrate chemistry a lot less tedious. It uses chemfig for drawing
the formulas. Different representation models (Fischer, Haworth, chair...) are
supported as well as alpha, beta, and chain isomers.

%package -n texlive-cases
Summary:        Numbered cases environment
Version:        svn77682
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cases-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cases-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-cases
This package provides a LaTeX environment "numcases" to produce multi-case
equations with a separate equation number for each case. There is also a
"subnumcases" environment which numbers each case with the overall equation
number plus a letter [8a, 8b, etc.].

%package -n texlive-casyl
Summary:        Typeset Cree/Inuktitut in Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics
Version:        svn15878
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-casyl-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-casyl-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-casyl
The bundle constitutes a font (as Metafont source) and LaTeX macros for its use
within a document.

%package -n texlive-catchfile
Summary:        Catch an external file into a macro
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(etexcmds.sty)
Requires:       tex(infwarerr.sty)
Requires:       tex(ltxcmds.sty)

%description -n texlive-catchfile
This package catches the contents of a file and puts it in a macro. It requires
e-TeX. Both LaTeX and plain TeX are supported.

%package -n texlive-catchfilebetweentags
Summary:        Catch text delimited by docstrip tags
Version:        svn21476
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-catchfilebetweentags-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-catchfilebetweentags-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(catchfile.sty)
Requires:       tex(etex.sty)
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(ltxcmds.sty)

%description -n texlive-catchfilebetweentags
This package (built using the facilities of catchfile) provides a macro
\catchfilebetweentags acts like the original \catchfile but only extracts a
portion of the file instead of the complete file. The extracted portion can be
delimited by strings or by docstrip tags: %<*tag> .... %</tag> (comments in the
caught region may be included or dropped).

%package -n texlive-catechis
Summary:        Macros for typesetting catechisms
Version:        svn59998
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-catechis-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-catechis-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(paralist.sty)

%description -n texlive-catechis
The macros include: format for question-and-answer; comments on answers;
lengthier explanations of answers; citations. The formatting of all the macros
is highly (and simply) customizable.

%package -n texlive-catoptions
Summary:        Preserving and recalling standard catcodes
Version:        svn68982
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-catoptions-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-catoptions-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(pdftexcmds.sty)

%description -n texlive-catoptions
The package changes package loading internals so that all subsequently loaded
packages can rely on normal/standard catcodes of all ASCII characters. The
package defines canonical control sequences to represent all the visible ASCII
characters. It also provides robust option parsing mechanisms (XDeclareOption,
XExecuteOptions and XProcessOptions, which will be used by \documentclass if
the package has already been loaded). The package also provides a range of
other TeX programming tools.

%package -n texlive-catppuccinpalette
Summary:        Provides (x)colors of catppuccin theme
Version:        svn75934
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(pgfopts.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)

%description -n texlive-catppuccinpalette
"Catppuccin" is a nice pastel theme in four flavours/styles (Latte, Frappe,
Macchiato, Mocha). This package defines these themes as xcolor colors.

%package -n texlive-cbcoptic
Summary:        Coptic fonts and LaTeX macros for general usage and for philology
Version:        svn16666
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cbcoptic-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cbcoptic-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(textcomp.sty)

%description -n texlive-cbcoptic
CBcoptic is a bundle of files for typesetting Coptic philological text with the
proper fonts and hyphenation. The fonts are based on, but much extend, the
fonts of the original coptic bundle. The CBcoptic bundle includes font
description files, Metafont sources and equivalent Adobe Type 1 fonts in pfb
format. The bundle also includes a package that provides some macros of
philological interest.

%package -n texlive-ccaption
Summary:        Continuation headings and legends for floats
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ccaption-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ccaption-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-ccaption
A package providing commands for 'continuation captions', unnumbered captions,
and also a non-specific legend heading for any environment. Methods are also
provided to define captions for use outside float (e.g., figure and table)
environments, and to define new float environments and Lists of Floats. Tools
are provided for specifying your own captioning styles.

%package -n texlive-cclicenses
Summary:        Typeset Creative Commons licence logos
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cclicenses-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cclicenses-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(rotating.sty)

%description -n texlive-cclicenses
The cclicenses package helps users typesetting Creative Commons logos in LaTeX.
It defines some commands useful to quickly write these logos, related to CC
licences versions 1.0 and 2.0.

%package -n texlive-cd
Summary:        Typeset CD covers
Version:        svn34452
License:        GPL-2.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cd-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cd-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-cd
Normal usage will ordinarily require no more than a simple data file per cover;
the package will make a full insert for a CD case (it copes with both normal
and slim cases).

%package -n texlive-cd-cover
Summary:        Typeset CD covers
Version:        svn17121
License:        GPL-2.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cd-cover-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cd-cover-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-cd-cover
The CD-cover class will typeset front and back cover sheets for CD jewel cases,
or an entire paper cover, or a label for a plastic slip-cover.

%package -n texlive-cdcmd
Summary:        Expandable conditional commands for LaTeX
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-cdcmd
This package provides some conditional commands, just like the styledcmd
package. The difference is that cdcmd can define expandable conditional
commands.

%package -n texlive-cdpbundl
Summary:        Business letters in the Italian style
Version:        svn61719
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cdpbundl-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cdpbundl-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(babel.sty)
Requires:       tex(color.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)

%description -n texlive-cdpbundl
The C.D.P. Bundle can be used to typeset high-quality business letters
formatted according to Italian style conventions. It is highly configurable,
and its modular structure provides you with building blocks of increasing
level, by means of which you can compose a large variety of letters. It is also
possible to write letters divided into sections and paragraphs, to include
floating figures and tables, and to have the relevant indexes compiled
automatically. A single input file can contain several letters, and each letter
will have its own table of contents, etc., independent from the other ones.

%package -n texlive-cellprops
Summary:        Accept CSS-like selectors in tabular, array, ...
Version:        svn76924
License:        GPL-3.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(mdwtab.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xparse.sty)

%description -n texlive-cellprops
This package reworks the internals of tabular, array, and similar constructs,
and adds a \cellprops command accepting CSS-like selectors and properties. It
depends on mdwtab, xcolor, expl3, and xparse.

%package -n texlive-cellspace
Summary:        Ensure minimal spacing of table cells
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-cellspace-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-cellspace-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(amsmath.sty)
Requires:       tex(array.sty)
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-cellspace
It is well known that high or deep cells tend to touch the \hlines of a
tabular. This package provides a modifier S acting on usual column types so
that to ensure a minimal distance that can be controlled through two parameters
\cellspacetoplimit and \cellspacebottomlimit. The approach employed by this
package is noticeably simpler than that of tabls, which considers the
dimensions of each entire row; whereas you can ask the cellspace only to look
at the cells of potentially difficult columns. The package depends on ifthen,
array, calc, and xkeyval.

%package -n texlive-censor
Summary:        Tools for producing redacted documents
Version:        svn74794
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-censor-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-censor-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(pbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(tokcycle.sty)

%description -n texlive-censor
This package provides simple tools for creating redacted documents with
blacked-out text. Its tools are useful both for creating documents in a
restricted environment (for redacted release in an unrestricted environment) as
well as in an unrestricted environment (for eventual transfer and completion in
the restricted environment).

%package -n texlive-centeredline
Summary:        A macro for centering lines
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-centeredline
This package provides a macro \centeredline{...} which allows to conveniently
center a line inside a paragraph while allowing usage therein of \verb or other
macros changing catcodes. It works nicely in list environments, and material
whose natural width exceeds the current linewidth will get properly centered
too.

%package -n texlive-centerlastline
Summary:        Paragraphs with last line centered, known as "Spanish" paragraphs
Version:        svn56644
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-centerlastline
This LaTeX package provides a command \centerlastline and an environment
centerlastline that typeset "Spanish" paragraphs, that is paragraphs without
indentation, and last line centered, useful to finish a large paragraph of text
at the end of chapters, prologues, etc.

%package -n texlive-changebar
Summary:        Generate changebars in LaTeX documents
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-changebar-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-changebar-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-changebar
Identify areas of text to be marked with changebars with the \cbstart and
\cbend commands; the bars may be coloured. The package uses 'drivers' to place
the bars; the available drivers can work with dvitoln03, dvitops, dvips, the
emTeX and TeXtures DVI drivers, and VTeX and pdfTeX.

%package -n texlive-changelayout
Summary:        Change the layout of individual pages and their text
Version:        svn16094
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-changelayout-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-changelayout-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(etextools.sty)
Requires:       tex(ltxnew.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-changelayout
The package is an extension of the changepage package to permit the user to
change the layout of individual pages and their texts.

%package -n texlive-changelog
Summary:        Typesetting keepachangelog.com style changelogs
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(translations.sty)

%description -n texlive-changelog
This package provides a changelog environment (which itself provides a version
environment) to represent a changelog. The package supports multiple authors,
unreleased changes, and yanked (revoked) releases. Inspired by
keepachangelog.com.

%package -n texlive-changepage
Summary:        Margin adjustment and detection of odd/even pages
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-changepage-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-changepage-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-changepage
The package provides commands to change the page layout in the middle of a
document, and to robustly check for typesetting on odd or even pages.
Instructions for use are at the end of the file. The package is an extraction
of code from the memoir class, whose user interface it shares. It is intended
the this package will eventually replace the chngpage package, which is
distributed with the package.

%package -n texlive-changes
Summary:        Manual change markup
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-changes-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-changes-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(todonotes.sty)
Requires:       tex(truncate.sty)
Requires:       tex(ulem.sty)
Requires:       tex(xcolor.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)
Requires:       tex(xstring.sty)

%description -n texlive-changes
The package allows the user to manually markup changes of text, such as
additions, deletions, or replacements. Changed text is shown in a different
color; deleted text is striked out. Additionally, text can be highlighted
and/or commented. The package allows free definition of additional authors and
their associated color. It also allows you to change the markup of changes,
authors, highlights or comments. A Python script is provided for removing the
changes.

%package -n texlive-chappg
Summary:        Page numbering by chapter
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-chappg-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-chappg-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-chappg
The package provides for 'chapterno-pageno' or 'chaptername-pageno' page
numbering. Provision is made for front- and backmatter in book class.

%package -n texlive-chapterfolder
Summary:        Package for working with complicated folder structures
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-chapterfolder-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-chapterfolder-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)

%description -n texlive-chapterfolder
This package simplifies working with folder structures that match the
chapter/section/subsection structure. It provides macros to define a folder
that contains the file for a chapter/section/subsection, and provides macros
that allow inclusion without using the full path, rather the path relative to
the current folder of the chapter/section/subsection. It makes easy changing
the name of a folder, for example.

%package -n texlive-cheatsheet
Summary:        A simple cheatsheet class
Version:        svn45069
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-cheatsheet
The package provides a clean, multi-column design intended for cheat sheets. It
imports the most useful packages and encloses the document in a multicol
environment.

%package -n texlive-checkend
Summary:        Extend "improperly closed environment" messages
Version:        svn78101
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-checkend
When an environment is left open, LaTeX gives an error at the end of the
document. However it only informs about the first of them, while the rest are
shown with meaningless errors: (\end occurred inside a group at level N) This
package replaces these errors with more useful messages which show which
environments (in reverse order) were not closed. There are no user macros: just
use the package.

%package -n texlive-chet
Summary:        LaTeX layout inspired by harvmac
Version:        svn78825
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-chet-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-chet-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(amsmath.sty)
