%description -n texlive-easyreview
The easyReview package provides a way to review (or perform editorial process)
in LaTeX. You can use the provided commands to claim attention in different
ways to part of the text, or even to indicate that a text was added, needs to
be removed, needs to be replaced and add comments to the text.

%package -n texlive-ebezier
Summary:        Device independent picture environment enhancement
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ebezier-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ebezier-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(calc.sty)

%description -n texlive-ebezier
Ebezier is a device independent extension for the standard picture environment.
Linear, quadratic, and cubic bezier curves are supplied in connection with
higher level circle drawing commands. Additionally some macros for the
calculation of curve lengths are part of this package.

%package -n texlive-ecclesiastic
Summary:        Typesetting Ecclesiastic Latin
Version:        svn38172
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ecclesiastic-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ecclesiastic-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(iftex.sty)

%description -n texlive-ecclesiastic
The package modifies the way the latin option to babel operates when
typesetting Latin. The style is somewhat 'frenchified' in respect of
punctuation spacings and footnote style; shortcuts are available in order to
set accents on all vowels, including y and the diphthongs ae and oe.

%package -n texlive-econlipsum
Summary:        Generate sentences from economic articles
Version:        svn77682
