breaking and improved math mode. It also patches some fancyvrb internals. Parts
of fvextra were originally developed as part of pythontex and minted.

%package -n texlive-fwlw
Summary:        Get first and last words of a page
Version:        svn77682
License:        fwlw
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-fwlw-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-fwlw-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-fwlw
The package extracts the first and last words of a page, together with the
first word of the next page, just before the page is formed into the object to
print. The package defines a couple of page styles that use the words that have
been extracted.

%package -n texlive-g-brief
Summary:        Letter document class
Version:        svn77050
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-g-brief-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-g-brief-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-g-brief
Designed for formatting formless letters in German; can also be used for
English (by those who can read the documentation). There are LaTeX 2.09
documentstyle and LaTeX2e class files for both an 'old' and a 'new' version of
g-brief.

%package -n texlive-gatherenum
Summary:        A crossover of align* and enumerate
Version:        svn76924
License:        GPL-3.0-or-later
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(enumitem.sty)
Requires:       tex(xparse.sty)

%description -n texlive-gatherenum
This package (ab)uses the inline enumeration capabilities of enumitem to add a
"displayed" enumeration mode, triggered by adding 'gathered' to the key-value
option list of the enumerate environment. The end result is similar to a
regular enumerate environment wrapped in a multicols environment, with the
following advantages: Gathered enumerate can pack items depending on their
actual width rather than a fixed, constant number per line. Gathered
enumeration fills items in a line-major order (instead of column-major order),
which my students found less confusing. YMMV. The package depends on enumitem,
expl3, and xparse,

%package -n texlive-gauss
Summary:        A package for Gaussian operations
Version:        svn32934
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-gauss-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-gauss-doc <= 11:%{version}
