%description -n texlive-getitems
This package provides a \gatheritems command to parse a list of data separated
by \item tokens. This makes it easier to define custom environments which
structure their data in the same way that itemize or enumerate do.

%package -n texlive-gindex
Summary:        Formatting indexes
Version:        svn52311
License:        MIT
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-gindex
This package provides a way to generate the format of index entries from within
LaTeX.

%package -n texlive-ginpenc
Summary:        Modification of inputenc for German
Version:        svn24980
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ginpenc-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ginpenc-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-ginpenc
If the inputenc is used and German umlauts are input directly, they are
converted to the LICR representation \"a (etc.). This breaks the sort algorithm
of makeindex, for instance. Ginpenc converts umlauts and the sharp-s to the
short forms defined by babel, e.g., "a instead, if the text is typeset in
German.

%package -n texlive-gitfile-info
Summary:        Get git metadata for a specific file
Version:        svn51928
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(currfile.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(tcolorbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(xparse.sty)

%description -n texlive-gitfile-info
If you are using git to control versions of LaTeX-files, you may want to show
yourself or other users or devs the current version of the file, information
about the author and last edited date. All packages for git known make that
kind of information available for the whole repository. But sometimes you have
a lot of files within the same repository in different versions, from different
authors etc. Perhaps you also split up a big project in small files and want to
show within the document who had edited what. This package gives you the
opportunity to do so.

%package -n texlive-gitinfo
Summary:        Access metadata from the git distributed version control system
Version:        svn34049
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-gitinfo-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-gitinfo-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(kvoptions.sty)
Requires:       tex(xstring.sty)

%description -n texlive-gitinfo
The package makes it possible to incorporate git version control metadata into
documents. For memoir users, the package provides the means to tailor page
headers and footers to use the metadata. Note this version is now deprecated,
but is kept on the archive, pro tem, for continuity for existing users. All new
repositories should use gitinfo2.

%package -n texlive-gitinfo2
Summary:        Access metadata from the git distributed version control system
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
