%description -n texlive-lengthconvert
The package provides a command to convert a length to any of a large selection
of units. The package relies on the LaTeX3 programming environment.

%package -n texlive-leporello
Summary:        A simple LaTeX document class to create folded leaflets using columns and boxes
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-leporello
A simple LaTeX document class to create folded leaflets with the following key
features: The document layout consists of a specific number of pages that can
have varying widths and are placed next to each other. Each page contains one
frame to contain typeset material. Material is typeset in boxes, and boxes are
positioned in columns which in turn are placed into the frames on the pages of
the document. Columns are predefined and then placed into the frame of a page
in the document layout. This way, columns can be used on pages with varying
widths. Boxes can have padding (including bleed) and a background and are
positioned inside a column.

%package -n texlive-lettre
Summary:        Letters and faxes in French
Version:        svn54722
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-lettre-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-lettre-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-lettre
Developed from the ancestor of the standard letter class, at the Observatoire
de Geneve.

%package -n texlive-lettrine
Summary:        Typeset dropped capitals
Version:        svn77053
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-lettrine-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-lettrine-doc <= 11:%{version}
