%package -n texlive-metre
Summary:        Support for the work of classicists
Version:        svn18489
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-metre-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-metre-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(relsize.sty)

%description -n texlive-metre
The package provides classicists with some of the tools that are needed for
typesetting scholarly publications dealing with Greek and Latin texts, with
special emphasis on Greek verse. As the package's name suggests, its core is a
comprehensive set of commands for generating metrical schemes and for placing
prosodical marks on text set in the Latin or the Greek alphabet. The rest of
the package provides a miscellany of commands for symbols (most of them not
directly related to metre) that are often used in critical editions of
classical texts. The package does not require any special font: all symbols are
taken from the Computer Modern fonts (which are included in all TeX
distributions) and the package's commands are based on TeX primitives.

%package -n texlive-mfirstuc
