\mruletv (vertical rules), and \undernote (underlined annotations). Key
Features: Key-Value Interface: All commands support a consistent key-value
syntax for adjust dimensions (width, height, depth), colors, and dash patterns
(dash, dash-len, gap-len). Underline Annotations: The \undernote command allows
users to attach descriptive notes to underlined text. It automatically handles
positioning, spacing between multiple notes, and provides options for various
border styles (solid or dashed boxes). Vertical Writing Compatibility: Designed
with multilingual typesetting in mind, the package is compatible with vertical
writing modes, ensuring that rules and notes are oriented correctly.
Customization: Users can update package-wide dfaults at any point in the
document using a dedicated set of \SetUNote... commands.

%package -n texlive-moderntimeline
