%description -n texlive-ocg-p
The package provides OCG (Optional Content Groups) support within a PDF
document, replacing the ocg.sty distributed with asymptote. Nested OCGs are
supported. The package may be used with pdfLaTeX and XeLaTeX.

%package -n texlive-ocgx
Summary:        Use OCGs within a PDF document without JavaScript
Version:        svn54512
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ocgx-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ocgx-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ocg-p.sty)

%description -n texlive-ocgx
The package extends the ocg package, which allows you to create OCGs (Optional
Content Groups) in PDF documents. (The ocg package is distributed as part of
Asymptote.) Every OCG includes TeX material into a layer of the PDF file. Each
of these layers can be displayed or not. Links can enable or disable the
display of OCGs. The ocgx package does not use Javascript embedded in the PDF
document to enable (to show) or disable (to hide) OCGs.

%package -n texlive-ocgx2
Summary:        Drop-in replacement for 'ocgx' and 'ocg-p'
Version:        svn78793
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-ocgx2-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-ocgx2-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(ocgx.sty)
Requires:       tex(pdfbase.sty)
Requires:       tex(tikz.sty)

%description -n texlive-ocgx2
This package serves as a drop-in replacement for the packages ocgx by Paul
Gaborit and ocg-p by Werner Moshammer for the creation of PDF Layers. It
re-implements the functionality of the ocg, ocgx, and ocg-p packages and adds
support for all known engines and back-ends including: LaTeX - dvips -
ps2pdf/Distiller (Xe)LaTeX(x) - dvipdfmx pdfLaTeX and LuaLaTeX . It also
ensures compatibility with the media9 and animate packages.

%package -n texlive-ocr-latex
Summary:        LaTeX support for ocr fonts
Version:        svn15878
