Requires:       tex(geometry.sty)
Requires:       tex(graphicx.sty)
Requires:       tex(grffile.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(kvoptions.sty)
Requires:       tex(tikz.sty)
Requires:       tex(twoopt.sty)
Requires:       tex(ulem.sty)
Requires:       tex(xstring.sty)

%description -n texlive-pdfreview
This package lets you add comments in the page margins of PDF files, e.g. when
reviewing manuscripts or grading reports. The PDF file to be annotated is
included, one page at a time, as graphics, in a manner similar to the pdfpages
package. Notes are placed in the margin next to the included graphics using a
grid of help lines. Alternatively, only numbers are placed in the page margins,
and the notes are collected into a numbered list at the end of the document.
Note that this package is not intended for adding notes directly to the LaTeX
source of the document that is being reviewed; instead, the document undergoing
review is already in PDF format and remains unchanged. Also note that this
package does not produce the usual PDF "sticky notes" that must be opened by
clicking on them; instead, the notes are simply shown as text. This package
depends on the following other LaTeX package: adjustbox, calc, geometry,
graphicx, grffile, ifthen, kvoptions, tikz, ulem, and xstring.

