Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       tex(scrtime.sty)

%description -n texlive-prelim2e
Puts text below the normal page content (the default text marks the document as
draft and puts a timestamp on it). Can be used together with e.g. the vrsion,
rcs and rcsinfo packages. Uses the everyshi package and can use the scrtime
package from the koma-script bundle.

%package -n texlive-preprint
Summary:        A bundle of packages provided "as is"
Version:        svn30447
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-preprint-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-preprint-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-preprint
The bundle comprises: authblk, which permits footnote style author/affiliation
input in the \author command, balance, to balance the end of \twocolumn pages,
figcaps, to send figure captions, etc., to end document, fullpage, to set
narrow page margins and set a fixed page style, and sublabel, which permits
counters to be subnumbered.

%package -n texlive-pressrelease
Summary:        A class for typesetting press releases
Version:        svn35147
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-pressrelease-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-pressrelease-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(marvosym.sty)
Requires:       tex(tikz.sty)

%description -n texlive-pressrelease
A configurable class for writing press releases.

%package -n texlive-prettyref
Summary:        Make label references "self-identify"
Version:        svn77682
License:        LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-prettyref-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-prettyref-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-prettyref
Prettyref provides a command \newrefformat, which specifies the way in which a
reference is typeset, according to a label "identification". The identification
is set in the \label command, by using prefixed label names; so instead of
\label{mysection}, one uses \label{sec:mysection}, and prettyref interprets the
"sec:" part. The package is compatible with hyperref and with other packages.

%package -n texlive-prettytok
Summary:        Pretty-print token lists
Version:        svn76924
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Requires:       texlive-filecontentsdef
Requires:       texlive-l3kernel
Requires:       texlive-precattl
Requires:       tex(precattl.sty)

%description -n texlive-prettytok
Pretty-print token lists to HTML file for debugging purposes. Open the file in
any browser to view the result. Can be used to replace \tl_analysis_show:n.

%package -n texlive-printlen
Summary:        Print lengths using specified units
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-printlen-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-printlen-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-printlen
\printlength{length} prints the value of a LaTeX length in the units specified
by \uselengthunit{unit} ('unit' may be any TeX length unit except for scaled
point, viz., any of: pt, pc, in, mm, cm, bp, dd or cc). When the unit is pt,
the printed length value will include any stretch or shrink; otherwise these
are not printed. The 'unit' argument may also be PT, in which case length
values will be printed in point units but without any stretch or shrink values.

%package -n texlive-probsoln
Summary:        Generate problem sheets and their solution sheets
Version:        svn44783
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-probsoln-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-probsoln-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(amsmath.sty)
Requires:       tex(etoolbox.sty)
Requires:       tex(ifthen.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-probsoln
The package is designed for lecturers who have to generate new problem sheets
for their students on a regular basis (e.g. yearly) by randomly selecting a
specified number of problems defined in another file. The package allows you
easily to generate a new problem sheet that is different from the previous
year, thus alleviating the temptation of students to seek out the previous
year's students and checking out their answers. The solutions to the problems
can be defined along with the problem, making it easy to generate the solution
sheet from the same source code; problems may be reused within a document, so
that solutions may appear in a different section of the same document as the
problems they cover.

%package -n texlive-profmaquette
