Requires:       tex(psfrag.sty)
Requires:       tex(shellesc.sty)
Requires:       tex(suffix.sty)
Requires:       tex(trimspaces.sty)
Requires:       tex(xkeyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-pstool
The package works in the same sort of way as pst-pdf, but it also processes the
PostScript graphics with psfrag to add labels within the graphic, before
conversion. Thus the bundle replaces two steps of an ordinary workflow.
(Naturally, the package requires that \write 18 is enabled.) Pstool ensures
that each version of each graphic is compiled once only (the graphic is
(re-)compiled only if it has changed since the previous compilation of the
document). This drastically speeds up the running of the package in the typical
case (though the first run of any document is inevitably just as slow as with
any similar package).

%package -n texlive-pstring
Summary:        Typeset sequences with justification pointers
Version:        svn42857
