Requires:       tex(graphicx.sty)
Requires:       tex(hyperref.sty)
Requires:       tex(inputenc.sty)
Requires:       tex(keyval.sty)

%description -n texlive-ucs
The bundle provides the ucs package, and utf8x.def, together with a large
number of support files. The utf8x.def definition file for use with inputenc
covers a wider range of Unicode characters than does utf8.def in the LaTeX
distribution. The package provides facilities for efficient use of its large
sets of Unicode characters. Glyph production may be controlled by various
options, which permits use of non-ASCII characters when coding mathematical
formulae. Note that the bundle previously had an alias "unicode"; that alias
has now been withdrawn, and no package of that name now exists.

%package -n texlive-uebungsblatt
Summary:        A LaTeX class for writing exercise sheets
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-uebungsblatt-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-uebungsblatt-doc <= 11:%{version}
Requires:       tex(akkcounterlabelpattern.sty)
Requires:       tex(fancyhdr.sty)
Requires:       tex(inputenc.sty)

%description -n texlive-uebungsblatt
This package implements a LaTeX class for writing exercise sheets for a
lecture. Features: - quick typesetting of exercise sheets or their revisions, -
simple user friendly commands, - elegant page formatting, - automatic numbering
of exercises and sub-exercises, - the number of the exercise sheet is extracted
automatically from the file name, - static information about the lectures and
the authors needs to provided at one point only.

%package -n texlive-ullrcorners
Summary:        Draw corners on the upper left and lower right sides of a word
Version:        svn75278
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea

%description -n texlive-ullrcorners
The package provides a command to surround a word or a sequence or words by
small corners on the upper left and lower right sides. The typographical
convention is inspired by Mastering Regular Expressions, by Jeffrey E. F.
Friedl (O'Reilly Media, 2006), where it is used to delimit regular expressions.

%package -n texlive-umoline
Summary:        Underline text allowing line breaking
Version:        svn19085
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-umoline-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-umoline-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-umoline
Provides commands \Underline, \Midline and \Overline for underlining, striking
out, and overlining their text arguments.

%package -n texlive-underlin
Summary:        Underlined running heads
Version:        svn15878
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-underlin-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-underlin-doc <= 11:%{version}

%description -n texlive-underlin
Defines two pagestyles that provide underlined page heads in LaTeX.

%package -n texlive-underoverlap
Summary:        Position decorations over and under expressions
Version:        svn77682
License:        LPPL-1.3c
Requires:       texlive-base
Requires:       texlive-kpathsea
Provides:       texlive-underoverlap-doc = %{epoch}:%{version}-%{release}
Obsoletes:      texlive-underoverlap-doc <= 11:%{version}
